---
// Visible, auditable marker for pages that do not yet carry final copy.
// REQ-001 §1.3: no placeholder may reach production. This component makes
// that easy to grep for (`PlaceholderNotice`) and easy to see on the page.
//
// R-9.1 AC2: the amber warning colours below were three raw hex literals
// in this component, which is exactly what AC2 forbids — a brand change
// could never have reached them. They now come from --warn-* in the token
// source in BaseLayout.astro. The brand sheet defines no status palette at
// all (it is a logo sheet, not a design system), so these are carried over
// unchanged rather than re-invented; moving them into the token source is
// what makes them changeable in one place when a status palette is decided.
---

<p class="placeholder-notice" data-placeholder="true">
	<strong>Placeholder —</strong> final content pending owner-supplied copy.
	Not for production.
</p>

<style>
	.placeholder-notice {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		border: 1px dashed var(--warn-line);
		background: var(--warn-surface);
		color: var(--warn-ink);
		padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-sm);
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
	}
</style>
